{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1504820-for-fun-most-useless-spells-for-attainments","id":1504820,"title":"[For Fun] Most Useless Spells for Attainments","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-03-08T00:54:35-08:00","id":1504820,"title":"[For Fun] Most Useless Spells for Attainments","content":"There's a few spells that are easy go-tos for Attainments - <u>Levitate</u>, direct damage spells, <u>Scrying</u>, <u>Acceleration</u>, <u>Shifting Sands</u>, etc. But what are some spells that are either impossible to make into a functional Attainment, or have such narrow uses that it isn't worth it?<br /> <br /> My first thought is <u>Dream Reaching</u>. It needs so much Reach to be used against other people, and off-hand I can't think of any good limitations you could add for more leeway that wouldn't cripple it worse. It might be a nice self-only Attainment, but it's so <i>pointless</i> as one, unless you add extra effects like free dots of Dream or Astral Adept","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 03-08-2023, 03:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-10T16:07:23-08:00","id":1505068,"title":"","content":"Unflagged!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-10T17:06:04-08:00","id":1505072,"title":"","content":"<i>Dream Reaching</i> has its uses when made into part of a toolkit. Lets say its combined with <i>Memory Hole</i> so the target forgets they were put to sleep, <i>Sleep of the Just </i>to put them asleep instantly and then <i>Hallucination </i>cast in ritual time so they can ignore the sense of their bodies. This Attainment suite creates a Lotus Eater Machine, where the subject will wither away without knowing it, similar to the cave dream in <i>Reign of the Exarchs</i>. It can be used by Guardians/Seers to perform More Than Brainwashing over an extended period of time or, if combined with Prime, keep a mage in a cage whose bars they can't even perceive.<br /> <br /> This combo is how I imagine an Arrow or Guardian would engineer a Kobayashi Maru style scenario to test the character of the subject, like whether someone is worthy of passing the Black Veil, joining a particular Legacy that involves high stress (Awakened Gambit) or highly sensitive information (Eleventh Question), or even being selected to guard a section of the Censorea.<br /> <br /> I think <i>Lodestone</i> is not useful enough as an Attainment. Its discrete enough in most cases, there is plenty of Reach available and its unlikely to be a great help in an emergency.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-10T18:00:48-08:00","id":1505078,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1504820-for-fun-most-useless-spells-for-attainments?p=1505072#post1505072\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Dream Reaching</i> has its uses when made into part of a toolkit. Lets say its combined with <i>Memory Hole</i> so the target forgets they were put to sleep, <i>Sleep of the Just </i>to put them asleep instantly and then <i>Hallucination </i>cast in ritual time so they can ignore the sense of their bodies. This Attainment suite creates a Lotus Eater Machine, where the subject will wither away without knowing it, similar to the cave dream in <i>Reign of the Exarchs</i>. It can be used by Guardians/Seers to perform More Than Brainwashing over an extended period of time or, if combined with Prime, keep a mage in a cage whose bars they can't even perceive.</div> </div> </div> </div>Most of those occupy the same cluster of levels though - <u>Dream Reaching</u> needs to swap Potency and Duration to see much use, plus it would need to be Instant Casting. <u>Sleep of the Just</u> is already a Disciple spell, and needs to swap Potency and Duration, be cast instantly, and be at Sight Range if you don't want to risk Aimed missing. <u>Hallucination</u> works fine in the Adept slot, I suppose, but with Sleep of the Just it will need to be in the Master slot. Which, at that point, you may as well just cast all that as spells rather than hope to have a Gnosis 8 Master to hand<br /> <br /> Its definately a good combo, but I don't see them working as Attainments.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think <i>Lodestone</i> is not useful enough as an Attainment. Its discrete enough in most cases, there is plenty of Reach available and its unlikely to be a great help in an emergency. </div> </div> </div>True. Most uses you'd put it to would be better served with <u>Alchemist's Touch</u>.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-12T03:03:17-07:00","id":1505167,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1504820-for-fun-most-useless-spells-for-attainments?p=1505072#post1505072\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Dream Reaching</i> has its uses when made into part of a toolkit. Lets say its combined with <i>Memory Hole</i> so the target forgets they were put to sleep, <i>Sleep of the Just </i>to put them asleep instantly and then <i>Hallucination </i>cast in ritual time so they can ignore the sense of their bodies. This Attainment suite creates a Lotus Eater Machine, where the subject will wither away without knowing it, similar to the cave dream in <i>Reign of the Exarchs</i>. It can be used by Guardians/Seers to perform More Than Brainwashing over an extended period of time or, if combined with Prime, keep a mage in a cage whose bars they can't even perceive.<br /> <br /> This combo is how I imagine an Arrow or Guardian would engineer a Kobayashi Maru style scenario to test the character of the subject, like whether someone is worthy of passing the Black Veil, joining a particular Legacy that involves high stress (Awakened Gambit) or highly sensitive information (Eleventh Question), or even being selected to guard a section of the Censorea.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really like this idea, thinking of optional Fate to guide the hallucinations/dreams to help awaken the target.<br /> <br /> Have a legacy focused on healing psychological trauma/personal growth, with the ultimate goal of enlightenment.<br /> <br /> Would Prime's purview of Truth be a better fit than Fate for the optional?<br /> <br /> Like you see past the lie in a Dream, but then you wake up, and eventually after repeated experiences you start to question whether your waking world is real...<br /> <br /> Mental note: must make an NPC for this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-12T09:19:33-07:00","id":1505175,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1504820-for-fun-most-useless-spells-for-attainments?p=1505167#post1505167\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I really like this idea, thinking of optional Fate to guide the hallucinations/dreams to help awaken the target.<br /> <br /> Have a legacy focused on healing psychological trauma/personal growth, with the ultimate goal of enlightenment.<br /> <br /> Would Prime's purview of Truth be a better fit than Fate for the optional?<br /> <br /> Like you see past the lie in a Dream, but then you wake up, and eventually after repeated experiences you start to question whether your waking world is real...<br /> <br /> Mental note: must make an NPC for this.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you, glad you liked it. I think Prime would be very useful, because it allow you to be discrete with your Nimbus (since mages on the downwards spiral may not even admit they have issues), detect the lies the patient tells themselves and create ways for them to physically interact with their mental issues.<br /> <br /> I also recommend looking at the <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1405749-new-legacy-oneiric-physicians\">Oneiric Physicians</a>, who are the closest thing to what you seem to be aiming towards.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 03-12-2023, 12:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-12T11:01:08-07:00","id":1505182,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1504820-for-fun-most-useless-spells-for-attainments?p=1505175#post1505175\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thank you, glad you liked it. I think Prime would be very useful, because it allow you to be discrete with your Nimbus (since mages on the downwards spiral may not even admit they have issues), detect the lies the patient tells themselves and create ways for them to physically interact with their mental issues.<br /> <br /> I also recommend looking at the <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1405749-new-legacy-oneiric-physicians\">Oneiric Physicians</a>, who are the closest thing to what you seem to be aiming towards.</div> </div> </div> </div>Was reminding me of this:<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/m/product/326243\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/m/img/dtrpg/m_icon_menu_cab.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/m/product/326243\" target=\"_blank\"> DriveThruRPG.com </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/m/product/326243\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.drivethrurpg.com/m/product/326243 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Your one-stop online shop for new and vintage RPG products from the top publishers, delivered fresh to your desktop in electronic format. </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Ebon Phoenix as seen in the Rookery Actual Play (Moros, Mind Primary, Death Optional legacy).<br /> <br /> I like the idea of messing with Dreams at one level, and then doing Hallucination at a higher level (the bring the Dreams out during wakefulness) as a way to help expose sleepers to the lie. So long as 'this is just a dream' doesn't result in trying to wake up via bridge jumping...<br /> <br /> Treating actual awakened patients is less fun, imo. Unless you have an Archmaster trying to help some Awakened along their Golden Roads... And i think Archmastery have gone beyond Legacies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-13T01:29:26-07:00","id":1505234,"title":"","content":"Psychic Domination.<br /> <br /> Like, take that as a one or two-dot Attainment, and your only Reach probably wants to go to Instant casting, meaning that all you get out of it is a one-word command that lasts seconds, only works on people with Resolve 1, and you need to touch the person to do it.<br /> <br /> Considerations do change a bit if you have it as a higher rated Attainment, mind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-13T02:23:16-07:00","id":1505239,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1504820-for-fun-most-useless-spells-for-attainments?p=1505234#post1505234\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Psychic Domination.<br /> <br /> Like, take that as a one or two-dot Attainment, and your only Reach probably wants to go to Instant casting, meaning that all you get out of it is a one-word command that lasts seconds, only works on people with Resolve 1, and you need to touch the person to do it.<br /> <br /> Considerations do change a bit if you have it as a higher rated Attainment, mind.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, absolutely useless at it's tier-level, but that's actually not too uncommon.<br /> <br /> You can squeeze a good deal out of it as a Master Attainment, although you basically have to choose two of; casting it instantly, casting it at Sight Range, or casting it with an Advanced Duration. The &quot;Any Order&quot; Reach effect is a must, but how it's being used will affect a lot.<br /> <br /> Instant Casting / Sight Range - Rapid-fire orders. &quot;Kill yourself&quot;, &quot;pull that lever&quot;, &quot;cut the rope&quot;, &quot;throw down your weapon&quot;, &quot;hands in the air&quot;<br /> <br /> Instant Casting / Advanced Duration - you're Talion in Shadow of Mordor. Slam your hand onto the target's face and yell &quot;SERVE ME&quot;. Vague, but effective.<br /> <br /> Sight Range /Advanced Duration - more subtle, but you spend an hour or so talking the target around to your way of thinking so they'll do the thing.<br /> <br /> If you can work in Time In A Bottle Utility Attainment (difficult, since my interpretation of the rules means Mind would need to be the Optional Attainments) then you can have all three. Or you take the slightly weaker &quot;Unwilling Orders&quot; rather than &quot;Any Order&quot; Reach effect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 03-13-2023, 05:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-13T17:20:21-07:00","id":1505269,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1504820-for-fun-most-useless-spells-for-attainments?p=1505239#post1505239\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You can squeeze a good deal out of it as a Master Attainment, although you basically have to choose two of</div> </div> </div> </div>Masters get four Reach for 2-dot spells.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The &quot;Any Order&quot; Reach effect is a must, but how it's being used will affect a lot.</div> </div> </div> </div>Depending on the personality of the Legacy.<br /> <br /> And indeed, how often one really needs to force people to take suicidal actions. Yields one more reach back to factors.<br /> <br /> Still, funny that lots of Reach in order to get the broadest range of utility out of it is acceptable for this but not for invading people's dreams.<br /> <br /> Which needs to be done with Instant casting because a sleeping person certainly can't spare a scene for having the Attainment cast in a ritual function.<br /> <br /> Indeed, I would think that the reduction of all ritual casting down to just one scene would afford a lot of latitude for Attainments to put their Reach into something other than casting time across the board.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-13T18:36:56-07:00","id":1505272,"title":"","content":"Maybe reflexive Suppress Life? I don\u2019t think corpse mimicry has much use, playing dead after a wound is cute but almost anything else is better. Might be good to spook people though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-13T18:39:51-07:00","id":1505273,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1504820-for-fun-most-useless-spells-for-attainments?p=1505269#post1505269\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Masters get four Reach for 2-dot spells.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right. Two to &quot;Any Order&quot;, two to spell factors. Or one to &quot;unwilling orders&quot;, three to spell factors. Which I covered.<br /> <br /> An addendum I'll make to my assessment though is the Mana Cost - &quot;Any Order&quot; adds a point of Mana to the cost, making it much less spam-friendly.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1504820-for-fun-most-useless-spells-for-attainments?p=1505269#post1505269\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Still, funny that lots of Reach in order to get the broadest range of utility out of it is acceptable for this but not for invading people's dreams.</div> </div> </div> </div>You think that's wierd? Have a look at <u>Devouring The Slain</u> and <u>Channel Mana</u> versus <u>Sacrificial Relinquishment</u>. It is, for some reason, several orders of magnitude easier to Attainment-ize killing something and making a spell self-sustaining than it is to Attainment-ize stealing Mana.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1504820-for-fun-most-useless-spells-for-attainments?p=1505269#post1505269\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which needs to be done with Instant casting because a sleeping person certainly can't spare a scene for having the Attainment cast in a ritual function.<br /> <br /> Indeed, I would think that the reduction of all ritual casting down to just one scene would afford a lot of latitude for Attainments to put their Reach into something other than casting time across the board.</div> </div> </div> </div>Er... I may be misunderstanding, but all Attainments already only take a Scene to cast, unless you sunk Reach into Instant Casting. <b>Page 198</b> - &quot;Most Attainments use one Reach for instant \u201ccasting\u201d; those that don\u2019t (being based on ritual spells) take one scene of preparation to use.&quot;<br /> <br /> Which isn't <i>\u200b\u200bimpossible</i> to use against a sleeping target, just inconvenient. \u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-14T11:26:08-07:00","id":1505345,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1504820-for-fun-most-useless-spells-for-attainments?p=1505273#post1505273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Er... I may be misunderstanding, but all Attainments already only take a Scene to cast, unless you sunk Reach into Instant Casting. <b>Page 198</b> - &quot;Most Attainments use one Reach for instant \u201ccasting\u201d; those that don\u2019t (being based on ritual spells) take one scene of preparation to use.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>My references there are in response to your own statement that it <u>needs</u> to be Instant Casting, which would seem to be pivotal to the assertion that it would be useless as an Attainment because of how much Reach it requires.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which isn't <i>\u200b\u200bimpossible</i> to use against a sleeping target, just inconvenient. \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>A sleeping person has to be the absolute most convenient target of a ritual spell even when it requires several hours to cast. Reducing that time to a scene is just gravy.<br /> <br /> They're easily somebody you can touch, and you probably don't need to have it work on very many at once, so have it as a Third Attainment and you've got the Reach you need to switch primary factor and still make it advanced duration and you've got all you require (unless it's very important to the Legacy's thesis that you actually appear as a character in their dream).<br /> <br /> Really, I would think that the most dubious spells to have as Attainments are the actual five dot ones, because so little flexibility in their factors sharply limits how much can be practically accomplished with them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-14T13:58:21-07:00","id":1505374,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1504820-for-fun-most-useless-spells-for-attainments?p=1505345#post1505345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My references there are in response to your own statement that it <u>needs</u> to be Instant Casting, which would seem to be pivotal to the assertion that it would be useless as an Attainment because of how much Reach it requires.</div> </div> </div> </div>But I... didn't? I said that in the Master slot you can get the most use out of <u>Psychic Domination</u>\u200b, since it's a Reach-hungry spell. Unless you're talking about <u>Dream Reaching</u>? If so, that was a really jarring jump.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A sleeping person has to be the absolute most convenient target of a ritual spell even when it requires several hours to cast. Reducing that time to a scene is just gravy. </div> </div> </div>Certainly! As long as you aren't chanting ominously in Latin and ringing bells, or what have you. Having to be in the same room as a sleeping target means you have to avoid waking them, which as I said is more an inconvenience than an impossibility.\u200b\u200b<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They're easily somebody you can touch, and you probably don't need to have it work on very many at once, so have it as a Third Attainment and you've got the Reach you need to switch primary factor and still make it advanced duration and you've got all you require (unless it's very important to the Legacy's thesis that you actually appear as a character in their dream). </div> </div> </div>But it still comes down to <i>how </i>and <i>why</i> they'd use it. Kaiser's idea is neat and has merit, but otherwise having to spend an hour sitting beside a sleeping person to be able to influence their dreams isn't particularly useful. Maybe as a therapy aid, but that's a very narrow use. I suppose the argument could be made for each casting allowing the Mage to influence the subject's dreams whenever they sleep for the Duration, regardless of their range after casting... but again, <i>why</i>? <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Really, I would think that the most dubious spells to have as Attainments are the actual five dot ones, because so little flexibility in their factors sharply limits how much can be practically accomplished with them. </div> </div> </div>Mostly. Time, surprisingly, has some good options, as does Matter. Anything paired with those or Space get a bit more flexibility, thanks to the Adept Utility Attainments.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-14T14:00:52-07:00","id":1505375,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1504820-for-fun-most-useless-spells-for-attainments?p=1505272#post1505272\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe reflexive Suppress Life? I don\u2019t think corpse mimicry has much use, playing dead after a wound is cute but almost anything else is better. Might be good to spook people though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Let's see... Two Reach for Reflexive use... one for Advanced Duration... yep. Not worth the needed slot. It'd be a great way to play possum, but anything that's a threat and trying to kill you is probably going to try disposing of your &quot;corpse&quot; anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-14T20:07:40-07:00","id":1505408,"title":"","content":"Cleanse Pattern. It's already an absurdly situational spell \u2014 it interacts with the Mystery/Focused Mage Sight subsystem, which might not be prominent or even used at all in a chronicle. And even then, it doesn't require basically anything that would make it any more useful to be cast as an Attainment. It's presumably Lasting, doesn't require Potency at all and has no Mana costs. It does something so obtuse (in 1E terms, <i>subtle as hell</i>) that you could never think it would incur Dissonance, and since it requires absolutely no Reach beyond instant casting (and sensory range, at the most), you will hardly ever risk paradox casting it normally even as an improvised spell.<br /> <br /> Most of these arguments also work for having the spell as a Rote or Praxis, but if you do use the Focused Mage Sight subsystem frequently enough it could feasibly be useful to be able to cast it without the improvised spell Mana cost, if Prime isn't a Ruling Arcanum for you. That way you can save Mana for extra successes in Revelations, I guess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27775,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27775-konviction","user":"KonViction","date":". 03-14-2023, 11:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27775-konviction","name":"KonViction","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-14T21:02:34-07:00","id":1505411,"title":"","content":"<i>Scribe Grimoire</i> is pretty bad as an Attainment. It can only target one Rote at a time, and its pretty low level, so Reach is plentiful. Its also not common enough that you need to scribe a rote now, with perfect reliability.<br /> <br /> <i>Accelerate Growth</i> also doesn't offer too much immediacy and its duration primary. Even if you had a bioengineering Legacy with long term goals, such as iterating on nature until we adapt past the constraints of the Lie, spells like <i>Transform Life</i> are generally more useful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}